  "method": "Labelled blind, before `refit meta-graph` ran on these repositories, by reading every live (non-test, non-example) file of the packages that hold the send-API code at the pinned commit. A label is one request to graph.facebook.com that belongs to the WhatsApp Business Platform (Cloud API messages and media, phone numbers, business profile, templates, registration, subscribed apps, calling, coexistence) or the Messenger Platform (Send API, including Instagram messaging through graph.facebook.com, user profiles by PSID, Messenger profile, conversations, handover, attachments, templates). `lines` are the line its HTTP or helper call starts on and, where the URL is written on another line, that line. Left out: media downloads from the URL Meta returns, generic Graph calls (/me, Page reads, OAuth, debug_token, app subscriptions, resumable uploads, catalogs), graph.instagram.com, and the bodies of generic request helpers whose callers are labelled.",
